From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sylvester Kaczmarek
 <16242628+sylvesterkaczmarek@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:36:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-modeset: map HDMI DSC max slices code 7 back to 16
 slices at 400 MHz

615.71.09 changed code 7 of the HDMI Forum VSDB DSC_MaxSlices field to 12 slices at
600 MHz. The HDMI DSC throughput path only knows the 400 MHz class and otherwise falls
back to 340 MHz, so sinks with this code lost modes. Restore the 610.57.04 mapping,
which is also what the kernel's drm_edid.c uses for it, and leave the new code 8 alone.

Upstream PR 1352 (Sylvester Kaczmarek). Fixes upstream issue 1348.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c b/src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c
index a54bd61a..ac24159f 100644
--- a/src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c
+++ b/src/common/modeset/timing/nvt_edidext_861.c
@@ -3911,7 +3911,7 @@ void parseEdidHdmiForumVSDB(VSDB_DATA *pVsdb, NVT_HDMI_FORUM_INFO *pHdmiInfo)
             switch(pHdmiForum->DSC_MaxSlices)
             {
             case 8: pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxSlices = 12; pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxPclkPerSliceMHz = 900; break;
-            case 7: pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxSlices = 12; pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxPclkPerSliceMHz = 600; break;
+            case 7: pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxSlices = 16; pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxPclkPerSliceMHz = 400; break;
             case 6: pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxSlices = 12; pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxPclkPerSliceMHz = 400; break;
             case 5: pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxSlices = 8;  pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxPclkPerSliceMHz = 400; break;
             case 4: pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxSlices = 8;  pHdmiInfo->dsc_MaxPclkPerSliceMHz = 340; break;
